From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphicscapture: Windows.Graphics.Capture -- capture items, frame pools, sessions, and the capture border.

GraphicsCaptureSession.IsSupported was FALSE and nothing else existed, so a
program sharing a window or the screen through Windows.Graphics.Capture (Zoom,
Teams, Discord, OBS's "Windows 10 (1903 and up)" capture) got nothing.
Implemented: GraphicsCaptureItem with IGraphicsCaptureItemInterop
CreateForWindow / CreateForMonitor (DisplayName, Size, Closed);
Direct3D11CaptureFramePool Create / CreateFreeThreaded (Recreate,
TryGetNextFrame, FrameArrived, CreateCaptureSession, IClosable);
GraphicsCaptureSession StartCapture, IsCursorCaptureEnabled, IsBorderRequired
and IClosable; Direct3D11CaptureFrame (Surface, ContentSize,
SystemRelativeTime). A session's thread reads the item's part of the screen
through the screen DC about sixty times a second -- the compositor's picture
under Stained Glass OS (winex11, 7857) -- draws the pointer when wanted, and
makes a changed picture the pool's next frame: a B8G8R8A8 texture of the
pool's device wrapped as an IDirect3DSurface (sgd3dinterop, 7854). While it
runs, the session's compositor draws Windows' yellow capture border round the
item (sg-compositor's CAPTUREBORDER, from graphicscapture.so); it is never in
the capture and goes with the session. Items, frame pools and sessions are
IWeakReferenceSource, as C++/WinRT event sources must be: OBS's capture
(libobs-winrt) took a weak reference to the item for its Closed handler and
crashed without one.
---
diff --git a/dlls/graphicscapture/Makefile.in b/dlls/graphicscapture/Makefile.in
index c17d4a4..a21ff64 100644
--- a/dlls/graphicscapture/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/graphicscapture/Makefile.in
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
 MODULE  = graphicscapture.dll
-IMPORTS = combase
+UNIXLIB = graphicscapture.so
+IMPORTS = combase dwmapi user32 gdi32
 
 SOURCES = \
+	capture.c \
 	classes.idl \
 	main.c \
-	session.c
+	session.c \
+	unixlib.c \
+	weakref.c
diff --git a/dlls/graphicscapture/capture.c b/dlls/graphicscapture/capture.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65d3d79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/graphicscapture/capture.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1641 @@
